    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Guardian Auto, which will dramatically change the way that both parents and teens drive a shared family car.  Drivers who are registered to drive the car at purchase open the car with a fingerprint scan on the driver door handle.  The scanner identifies the driver, opens a corresponding ‘driver profile,’ and initiates car features which have been enabled for the given driver.  If a guest needs to temporarily access the car, selected profiles can set up a numerical guest code, which would be entered by the guest into a keypad hidden on the inside of the car’s gas cover door.  The net result is a driving experience scaled to every driver’s safety needs.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
